WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.219
Step 1 of 9. Log a meeting from the “New” menu.

2
00:00:05.219 --> 00:00:09.081
Step 2 of 9. Choose who you met from your contacts.

3
00:00:09.081 --> 00:00:11.414
Step 3 of 9. Set when it happened (Melbourne time).

4
00:00:11.414 --> 00:00:16.674
Step 4 of 9. Search for the venue. Place search uses Photon on OpenStreetMap data, with a bundled Melbourne fallback.

5
00:00:16.674 --> 00:00:21.557
Step 5 of 9. The map flies to the venue and drops a pin you can drag or move with a click.

6
00:00:21.557 --> 00:00:33.154
Step 6 of 9. Add the notes, then log the meeting.

7
00:00:33.154 --> 00:00:40.778
Step 7 of 9. The meeting page: the pin, the distance from the CBD and the notes.

8
00:00:40.778 --> 00:00:47.950
Step 8 of 9. The records map: filter to the last 30 days and open the new meeting from the list.

9
00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:55.240
Step 9 of 9. The calendar: the same meeting on today's date.
